description:
Design a D flip-flop with asynchronous reset, set, and clear functionality. On the rising edge of the clock, if the reset signal is low, the output q is set to LOW. If the set signal is high, q is set to HIGH. If the clear signal is high, q is reset to LOW. If neither set nor clear signals are active, q takes the value of the data input d. This module is useful for implementing memory storage with additional control features for initialization and state management.
module top_module(
  input clk, rst, set, clr, d,
  output reg q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk, rst, set, clr, d,
  output reg q
);always @(posedge clk or negedge rst) begin
  if (~rst) begin
    q <= 1'b0;
  end else if (set) begin
    q <= 1'b1;
  end else if (clr) begin
    q <= 1'b0;
  end else begin
    q <= d;
  end
end

endmodule

