Design a 2-to-16 line decoder that converts two binary selection inputs (sel1 and sel0) into a unique one-hot output across 16 lines. Each output line will be activated based on the combination of the input selection signals, enabling one specific output while keeping all others low. The outputs represent all possible combinations of the input selection lines, providing a means to decode binary input into a wider output signal space.
