description:
Design a priority encoder that takes an 8-bit input and outputs the position of the highest active bit. The module first converts the binary input to Gray code for efficient bit handling, then converts it back to binary to determine the most significant active bit. The output is a 3-bit wide signal indicating the position of this active bit, with the highest priority given to the most significant bit. If no bits are active, the output is set to zero.
module top_module(
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [2:0] pos
);

