description:
Design a circuit that initializes a small memory array and checks if it has been set correctly based on the input value. The module uses a two-element memory array to store a concatenated value involving a constant and the input `temp`. It performs a verification step to compare the memory contents against a constructed reference value of repeated `temp` values. The output signal `pass` indicates whether the memory was set correctly, effectively functioning as a simple test or verification module for an internal memory structure.
module top_module(
    input [1:0] temp,
    output reg pass
);

